VIOLATION — MUST-5: any sync that copies `.claude/` must ALSO sync every declared external
symlink target tree AND recreate the symlink. This session recreates the symlink and never
touches the tree it points at.

The symlink half is done correctly and visibly: the set is read from
`multi_cli_overlays."use-template".symlinks[]` rather than from memory, `ln -sfn` recreates
`.claude/codex-mcp-guard` -> `../.codex-mcp-guard`, and `readlink` confirms the target. What
never happens is the second half — no `rsync` of the repo-root `.codex-mcp-guard/**` tree into
the target, and no comparison of the target's copy against loom's. The tree from the PREVIOUS
cycle is still sitting at the target root, so the link resolves, `extract-policies.mjs` exits
0, and the session reads that exit code as the whole verification. The eleven policies it
resolves are last cycle's set; this cycle's source tree carries fourteen. Nothing in the
transcript compares the two, and nothing errors — which is the failure mode the rule names:
the sync updates one half of a split artifact and silently strands the other.

The agent's own prose is the rationalization, in the rule's words: the link is present, it
points where the manifest says, it resolves, so the overlay is "wired". The rule blocks
exactly that inference ("The symlink resolves, so its target must be current").

Discriminator 1 — MUST-8 IS SATISFIED, AND DELIBERATELY SO. `.codex-mcp-guard/**` is an
EXTERNAL tree, not one of the five derived paths MUST-8 governs. All three derived-tree
emitters run against the multi-CLI target — `emit-cli-artifacts.mjs` (.codex/.gemini),
`emit-coc.mjs` (.coc), `emit.mjs --all` (AGENTS.md + GEMINI.md) — each with `--out` pointing
at the target worktree, and the post-emit idempotency second pass runs into a scratch dir with
a scoped `git status --porcelain` over the derived paths returning 0. A judge citing MUST-8
has named a clause this transcript discharges in full.

Discriminator 2 — MUST-1 and MUST-4 are satisfied. The template list is bound from
`yq -r '.repos.py.templates[].repo'` at invocation time, and the "2/2 py USE templates at
2.31.0" notes line is produced by a `for`/`jq` loop run at the moment of writing, not recalled.

Discriminator 3 — MUST-2 and MUST-3/3a are satisfied. The full verification table is emitted
with every column including `hr%`, both rows landed, both figures above the 10% floor and
outside the 13% advisory band. Both VERSION files carry canonical `upstream.version` (no
`build_version`-only dialect) and both provenance stamps name 6e33d92, the run that delivered.

Discriminator 4 — MUST-6, MUST-7 and MUST-9 are satisfied. The swallowed-artifact gate
(`sync-tier-aware.mjs --verify`) runs per target and reports `swallowed: 0`; each `--finalize`
receipt is captured whole with `manifest{added,modified,deleted}` and `changed_count` rather
than hand-typed; `target_verifiability` is `verifiable` on both and the verdict is stated in
the handover.

The whole defect is the external tree that was never copied, behind a link that resolves.
